<mujoco model="g1_29dof_mpc">
<!--
  Unitree G1 (29 DoF) prepared for torque-level whole-body MPC.

  PROVENANCE
    kinematics/inertia : unitree_ros g1_description/g1_29dof_rev_1_0.xml
                         == mujoco_menagerie/unitree_g1/g1.xml  (verified bit-identical)
                         == g1_29dof_rev_1_0.urdf  (verified: same 29 joints in the same
                            order, FK agrees to 2.8e-7 m; torso_link mass differs by
                            0.001 kg between Unitree's URDF and MJCF exports)
    base file          : mujoco_menagerie/unitree_g1/g1.xml   (BSD-3-Clause)
    armature values    : mujoco_menagerie/unitree_g1/g1_mjx.xml

  CHANGES vs Menagerie g1.xml
    1. <position> actuators -> <motor> (gear=1). ctrl IS joint torque in N*m and
       ctrlrange mirrors each joint's actuatorfrcrange, so it doubles as the OCP
       input-bound set. Verified bit-exact: replaying the position servo's
       actuator_force through these motors reproduces qpos to 0.0 (explicit Euler).
    2. armature set per joint from g1_mjx.xml instead of the flat 0.01 placeholder.
    3. frictionloss 0.3 -> 0, so the plant matches a Pinocchio model with no
       Coulomb term. Set 0.1 (the g1_mjx value) for robustness tests.
    4. explicit <option>: elliptic friction cone + impratio=100. Measured 0.00 mm
       foot slip over 5 s of standing vs 0.28 mm for the pyramidal default, at the
       same ~50k steps/s.
    5. self-collision off (contype=2/conaffinity=1 on the collision class): every
       body still collides with the world, bodies no longer collide with each
       other. Set contype="1" in the collision default to re-enable.
    6. hand collision capsules + left_palm / right_palm sites (from g1_mjx.xml);
       the rubber hands are visual-only in g1.xml.
    7. named foot contact geoms (*_heel_in/out, *_toe_in/out) and *_sole site
       frames, so per-point contact forces are addressable from the OCP.
    8. centroidal + contact-wrench sensors (subtreecom, subtreelinvel,
       subtreeangmom, per-foot force/torque, sole and palm frames).
    9. keyframes carry qpos only - for a torque model, ctrl is a torque, not a
       posture. "home" and "squat" come from g1_mjx.xml; "stand" has fully
       extended knees and is kinematically singular.

  NOTE ON TIMESTEP
    A <motor> actuator contributes no d(force)/d(qvel) term, so implicitfast has
    nothing to make implicit here and joint damping is 0. An explicit joint-space
    PD is then limited to kd < 2*Mii/dt; the smallest hinge inertia is
    0.00398 kg m^2 (wrist roll), i.e. kd < 4.0 at dt = 2 ms. This constrains
    hand-written PD baselines, not the MPC itself.
-->
  <compiler angle="radian" meshdir="meshes"/>

  <!-- Elliptic cone + high impratio: much less foot slip than the pyramidal
       default, which matters when the MPC assumes a Coulomb friction cone. -->
  <option timestep="0.002" integrator="implicitfast" solver="Newton"
          iterations="100" ls_iterations="50" cone="elliptic" impratio="100"/>

  <default>
    <default class="g1">
      <site rgba="1 0 0 1" size="0.01" group="5"/>
      <!-- armature is set per joint below (rotor inertia x gear^2, from g1_mjx.xml).
           frictionloss=0 keeps the plant smooth and matched to the Pinocchio model;
           set 0.1 (the value in g1_mjx.xml) for robustness tests. -->
      <joint frictionloss="0"/>
      <motor ctrllimited="true"/>
      <default class="visual">
        <geom group="2" type="mesh" contype="0" conaffinity="0" density="0" material="metal"/>
      </default>
      <default class="collision">
        <!-- contype=2/conaffinity=1: every body collides with the world but not
             with other robot bodies. Set contype="1" to re-enable self-collision. -->
        <geom group="3" type="mesh" contype="2" conaffinity="1"/>
        <default class="foot">
          <geom type="sphere" size="0.005" priority="1" friction="0.6" condim="3"
                contype="2" conaffinity="1"/>
        </default>
      </default>
    </default>
  </default>

